      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 British Society for Immunology.",
        "AbstractText": "A major goal in organ transplantation has been to safely exploit the natural processes of immune tolerance in order to minimize the dose and duration of drug immunosuppression. In this commentary, I argue that we can learn from how tumours avoid rejection, to evolve a three-stage tolerance-inducing strategy for transplanted tissues."
      },
